# G077 — Password Safe

*v2. See `password-safe.md` for prose: key lives only when unlocked,
zero-knowledge by design, lock/unlock as an FSM, auto-lock as a time-
triggered state transition, password generation and strength as
orthogonal concerns, verifier hash separate from key.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Agent Credential Retrieval

[agent-credential-use @target
    IN ORDER TO
        unlock the vault's credential safe with a user-prompted master
        look up the service's entry, fetch the decrypted password once
        and use it without ever logging or emitting it as telemetry

    @safe   <- [safe[load {path: "~/.dpn-safe.enc"}]]
    @master <- [secret[prompt {title: "unlock credential safe"}]]

    [safe[unlock
           {safe: @safe, master: @master, now-ms: [clock[now]]}]]
        || -> #wrong-master (no retry storm — caller decides)

    @cred     <- [safe[search
                         {safe: @safe,
                          query: @target:service,
                          now-ms: [clock[now]]}]] first
    @password <- [safe[get-password
                         {safe: @safe,
                          id: @cred:id,
                          now-ms: [clock[now]]}]]

    [use-credential {password: @password, target: @target}]
    ;; @password never flows into logs / summaries / telemetry
]

---

## Verb Surface

[safe
    new                 {master, auto-lock-after-ms}
    load                {path}
    save                {safe, path}
    unlock              {safe, master, now-ms}       ;; || wrong-master
    lock                {safe}                        ;; wipes key from memory
    add-entry           {safe, service, username, password, notes, now-ms}
    get-summary         {safe, id, now-ms}            ;; metadata, no secret
    get-password        {safe, id, now-ms}            ;; secret, gated
    search              {safe, query, now-ms}         ;; returns summaries
    remove-entry        {safe, id, now-ms}
    generate-password   {policy, seed}
    password-strength   {pw}                          ;; works on any string
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: state gate as `where` locked-or-unlocked

[safe[get-password {safe: @s, id: @id, now-ms: @now}]
    IN ORDER TO
        return the decrypted password only when the safe is unlocked
        and auto-lock has not elapsed since last activity

    @s
        where state is "Unlocked"
        and (@now - @s:last-activity-ms) at most @s:auto-lock-after-ms
            -> decrypt @s:entries at @id with in-memory key
               and record @now as last activity
        where state is "Unlocked" but auto-lock elapsed
            -> [safe[lock {safe: @s}]]
               -> #auto-locked
        otherwise
            -> #locked (ciphertext is present but key is absent)
]

## Distinctive Innate idiom: metadata-readable, secret-gated `where` field is encrypted

[safe[search {safe: @s, query: @q, now-ms: @now}]
    returns summaries (service, username, notes) — plaintext fields
    IN ORDER TO
        let callers (and logs) see metadata without revealing any password
        so passwords never leak into scrollback, error text, or telemetry

    get-password is the ONLY verb that returns secret material
    every other read returns summaries only
]

Encrypting the service name hurts search without adding real security;
encrypting the password is load-bearing. Production managers split
the same way — selective encryption, not uniform encryption.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @s <- [safe[new {master: "correct-horse",
                      auto-lock-after-ms: 300000}]]
    [safe[add-entry
           {safe: @s, service: "github.com", username: "alice",
            password: "p4ssw0rd", notes: "work account",
            now-ms: 0}]]
    [safe[lock {safe: @s}]]

    -> [safe[get-password {safe: @s, id: 0, now-ms: 1000}]]
    ;; -> #locked

    [safe[unlock {safe: @s, master: "correct-horse", now-ms: 2000}]]
    -> [safe[get-password {safe: @s, id: 0, now-ms: 3000}]]
    ;; -> "p4ssw0rd"

    -> [safe[get-password {safe: @s, id: 0, now-ms: 600000}]]
    ;; -> #auto-locked (>300s since last activity)
]
